---

`prove -l t/spec_to_type.t` on `main`:

    not ok - no class differs from what lib/ ships      (got 201, expected 0)
    not ok - every compared class is identical          (got 0, expected 201)

Cause: `maint/spec-to-type.pl:67` carries `my $VERSION_LITERAL = '0.004';` and writes it into every generated class (`:421`). Commit `0996c90` ("increment $VERSION after 0.004 release", the bundle's bump-after-release step) rewrote all 201 `lib/API/Docker/Type/*.pm` to `0.005`. The only difference per class is that one line:

    perl maint/spec-to-type.pl --verify /tmp/x/out
    diff /tmp/x/out/.../AuthConfig.pm lib/API/Docker/Type/AuthConfig.pm
    3c3
    < our $VERSION = '0.004';
    > our $VERSION = '0.005';

So the byte-for-byte guard goes red after every release and stays red until someone edits the literal by hand; the test only runs in a checkout (it skips in a built dist), which is why the release itself did not notice.

Done: the generator takes the version from `lib/API/Docker.pm` (or the comparison ignores the `our $VERSION` line), `t/spec_to_type.t` is green on `main`, and a release bump no longer needs a manual edit in `maint/`.

